Pacman - a tribute to the 1980 maze game, in JavaScript
=======================================================

A personal, non-commercial tribute to Namco's 1980 arcade game.
Pac-Man is a trademark of Bandai Namco; this program is not connected
with them.

!Pacman, in the Diversions directory on the hard disc, is a maze game
after that arcade classic. You steer Pac-Man round a maze, eating the
dots, while a ghost chases you. The whole program is in the
application directory, as JavaScript you can read in !JsEdit and
change; it is built on GameLib, the library of game parts in
!Boot.Resources (see the GameLib guide).

This is the first version. It has the maze, the dots and energizers,
and one ghost, Blinky. The other three ghosts, the ghosts turning
blue, fruit, lives, levels, sounds, a settings page and high scores
are still to come, and parts 4 to 7 below will be written as they
arrive.

